  "title": "Return to Sender: The Grumman LLV Has Finally Reached the End of Its Mail Delivery Days",
  "summary": "The Grumman LLV—for Long Life Vehicle—mail truck is proof that sometimes federal bureaucrats get it right. The aluminum-bodied lump just completed four decades as the principal mail carrier for the United States Postal Service. The history of mail delivery is, of course, inextricably linked with the history of American transportation. Legal documents and love letters […]",
